script = ExtResource("1_p4esa")
dialogue_id = "debate_magic_fire"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Magic Rituals"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Back when the priests among our ancestors practiced magical rituals, they settled a shard we now call The Fox Spirits Domain.
historian: When they first met these foxes, they considered them evil spirits, and decided to banish them with fire and axe.
historian: Their descendants adopted fire as the solution to every inconvenience.
historian: If the spring pollen made them sneeze, they solved it by burning the forest down.
historian: It is a profound tragedy, how quickly a single act of misplaced zeal can become a tradition that leaves the world barren.
historian: We could look at their empty plains and conclude that people are doomed to destroy whatever they touch.
historian: But the people there do not burn forests anymore.
historian: They recognized the harm they were doing and changed their ways.
historian: They still keep the tradition alive, but instead of burning down forests, they build safe bonfires during festivals.
historian: This is the great strength of letting our people forge their own paths.
historian: They are allowed to make terrible mistakes, but they are also free to realize their folly and correct their course.
historian: If we bind all our shards to a single, unquestionable holy law, we lose the ability to change our minds."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
